      "writtenOn": "2025-06-24T10:47:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes agreed, I wanted to start a discussion upstream to see if conditional warning suppressions could be implemented. I think upstream dev had some plans to remove this warning, but re-added it while fixing another spurious warning:\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/all/9b23e4413873bee38961e628b0c73f6d3a26d494.1743799705.git.jpoimboe@kernel.org/\n\nI shall talk to them and see if we can hide this warning for genuine use cases like this. In the meantime, I can have a hacky patch to objtool to hide this warning. I thought it would be okay to have this warning for a while as it comes between a lot other warnings (ABI and such).",
      "parentUuid": "0fa45837_3249efb8",
      "revId": "e0c8ccef4f7c7a660983f3da88279d724a5187d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
